## Assemble the semantic core

The engine and editor share a pure model of fragment occurrences and safe rename
plans. Its complete module gathers the contracts, scanners, source mappings, and
validation developed in [Pure fragment symbols](symbols.html).

```ts : <<assemble pure fragment symbols.*>>= ./src/symbols.ts $
<<symbol contracts>>
<<symbol document validation>>
<<symbol occurrence construction>>
<<symbol fence collection>>
<<symbol inline scanner>>
<<symbol inline code scanner>>
<<symbol prose mapping>>
<<symbol table cell splitting>>
<<symbol table mapping>>
<<symbol table mentions>>
<<symbol document collection>>
<<symbol collection entry point>>
<<symbol rename validation>>
<<symbol rename preview>>
<<symbol rename safety>>
<<symbol rename planning>>
```

The headless engine combines its contracts, parsing rules, deterministic ordering,
templates, generation phases, and language projection input from
[The headless generation engine](engine.html).

```ts : <<assemble the headless generation engine.*>>= ./src/engine.ts $
<<engine interfaces and dependencies>>
<<engine publication identity>>
<<engine path and source validation>>
<<engine shared fragment scanning>>
<<engine shared header parsing>>
<<engine document ordering>>
<<engine template dependency discovery>>
<<engine project theme resolution>>
<<engine literal template substitution>>
<<engine default HTML template>>
<<engine generation orchestration>>
<<engine language collection>>
```

Safe persistence is a separate protocol. The module assembled below follows the
contracts, preparation, installation, rollback, and cleanup developed in
[Output transactions](output_transactions.html).

```typescript: <<assemble safe output transactions.*>>= src/output-transactions.ts $
<<transaction contracts>>
<<transaction directory error>>
<<transaction error>>
<<transaction state>>
<<transaction parents>>
<<transaction normalize>>
<<transaction preflight>>
<<transaction reserve>>
<<transaction create directory>>
<<transaction prepare>>
<<transaction install>>
<<transaction restore rename>>
<<transaction undo output>>
<<transaction rollback>>
<<transaction cleanup>>
<<transaction commit>>
```

## Assemble the host adapters

The command-line adapter combines terminal and filesystem boundaries with the
shared engine, publication runner, and transaction protocol developed in
[Command-line generation](cli.html).

```typescript: <<assemble the command-line adapter.*>>= src/cli.ts $
<<cli imports>>
<<cli output contract>>
<<cli usage>>
<<cli default IO>>
<<cli missing file predicate>>
<<cli relative path validation>>
<<cli filesystem inspection>>
<<cli transaction IO>>
<<cli document discovery>>
<<cli Pandoc runner>>
<<cli LaTeX plan>>
<<cli command lifecycle>>
```

Its executable boundary deliberately does nothing except pass process arguments
to the reusable runner.

```typescript: <<assemble the command-line entry point.*>>= src/cli-entry.ts $
import { run } from './cli';
void run(process.argv.slice(2)).then(code => { process.exitCode = code; });
```

The fixed-point verifier joins its public result with the staged verification
lifecycle explained in [Self-host verification](self_hosting.html).

```typescript: <<assemble self-host verification.*>>= src/self-hosting.ts $
<<self-host imports and result>>
<<self-host verification lifecycle>>
```


The VS Code entry point gathers the editor features discussed throughout the
editor chapters and applies the source template used by its generated module.

```ts : <<assemble the VS Code extension.*>>= ./src/extension.ts $ template=tssrc.template
/* Literate Programming by Nathan 'jesterKing' Letwory */

<<import necessary modules for literate>>
```

